    "body": "Review notes 1-3 and 5 are addressed in the stacked PR #805 (#792): the body-to-flange flare is enveloped by a 45° cone ending at the flange front, Weldon bodies carry a 1 mm radial clamp-screw allowance, the picker exposes the projection through the same undoable command, and every ER entry draws from one shared ER_SIZES table. The live shank check also reads the stored tool now. This PR stays as is; #805 changes two of its pinned numbers (the BT30 ER20 flare foot, the BT40 Weldon 12 mm flange band), explained in #805's body.",
